From: SaaiOS <os@saaios>
Subject: synaptics td4150: reset on resume when HDL is idle

Project-Xed (maazm7d/kernel_samsung_a12 HEAD 6d2c200) still has Samsung's
stock HDL shortcut. On SM-A127F a12s the IC is on-chip FW: in_hdl_mode
stays true after probe, host_downloading is already 0. Resume then:

  wait_hdl (always 100ms) → goto mod_resume

and never runs software CMD_RESET / identify / module reinit. IRQ 244
sticks at 7; REPORT_TOUCH never arrives.

RESET_ON_RESUME is commented out and only lives in the !in_hdl_mode
branch, so uncommenting it is a no-op on this unit.

Two sites in synaptics_tcm_core.c (td4150, not the unused generic
synaptics_tcm/ copy):

1. syna_tcm_resume: after wait_hdl succeeds, goto do_reset when
   host_downloading==0. Keep mod_resume only while a download is in flight.
2. syna_tcm_reset_and_reinit: do not skip identify + mod_cb->reinit when
   HDL is idle.

Applies with: patch -d os/third_party/kernel_samsung_a12 -p1 < this file

--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics/td4150/synaptics_tcm_core.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics/td4150/synaptics_tcm_core.c
@@ -2306,7 +2306,7 @@ static int syna_tcm_reset_and_reinit(struct syna_tcm_hcd *tcm_hcd,
 
 	/* for hdl, the remaining re-init process will be done */
 	/* in the helper thread, so wait for the completion here */
-	if (tcm_hcd->in_hdl_mode) {
+	if (tcm_hcd->in_hdl_mode && atomic_read(&tcm_hcd->host_downloading)) {
 		mutex_unlock(&tcm_hcd->reset_mutex);
 		kfree(resp_buf);
 
@@ -2706,7 +2706,12 @@ static int syna_tcm_resume(struct device *dev)
 				"Failed to wait for completion of host download\n");
 			goto exit;
 		}
-		goto mod_resume;
+		/* On-chip FW: in_hdl_mode stays set but download is idle.
+		 * Skip reset only while a host download is actually in flight.
+		 */
+		if (atomic_read(&tcm_hcd->host_downloading))
+			goto mod_resume;
+		goto do_reset;
 	} else {
 
 #ifdef RESET_ON_RESUME
